== 7. Residual risk: where the guarantee stops ==
  [LIMIT] a forger who holds the signing key AND replaces every retained copy produces history that verifies as consistent - NOT a success of the control; the signing key and the reviewer's retained copy must stay out of reach of whoever can edit the run directory
  timing channel (stub model, held-out, n=200 per setting per execution, 3 complete executions; chance = 0.50): no padding accuracy 0.795/0.795/0.800; 250 ms buckets 0.530/0.555/0.495 (pooled 0.527 over n=600)
  reading: padding takes this classifier from ~0.80 to a level not distinguishable from chance at a cost of ~200 ms per answered request; a leak is not ruled out (verdict at 250 ms: no leak detected (inconclusive as to absence); one weak classifier, constant-latency stub; see VALIDATION_ADDENDUM section 4).
  other documented limits: containers share the host kernel; local demo tokens, not SSO; JSON files, single host;
  the stub is not an LLM (see evidence/validation_2026-10-22/model_experiments.json for the optional real-model test).

